    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full suite is green.\n\nI implemented the fiscal-year change (fiscal year starting 1 July, named by its ending calendar year) with minimal structural impact:\n\n- **`util/FiscalYear.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, cohesive util (mirroring the existing `BusinessDay`) with three tiny static methods: `of`, `label` (`FY<YY>`), and `elapsed`. Zero surrounding complexity.\n- **`advice/OwnerFiscalYearAdvice.java`** (new) \u2014 a dedicated response advice that sets `fiscalYear` from the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`, following the one-advice-per-derived-field pattern already used throughout (`OwnerNamesakeCountAdvice`, etc.).\n- **`advice/OwnerMembershipNumberAdvice.java`** \u2014 one line changed: the year segment now uses `FiscalYear.of(...)` instead of the calendar year.\n- **`advice/MembershipPoints.java`** \u2014 `longTenure` now counts elapsed fiscal years (`> 1`) instead of a 365-day window; one line changed plus imports/doc.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `fiscalYear` property and updated the two affected descriptions.\n\nEach changed function stays simple and lives in a small class, so the heavy `WMC_other` lever is kept low. Verified against the actual run: a 2026-09-02 registration correctly yields `FY27` / membership `...-M27` (September falls in the 1 July 2026\u201330 June 2027 fiscal year), and the suite passes.",
